hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"776","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who asks her husband for divorce without any harm, the fragrance of Paradise is forbidden to her."
"777","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: And from what I read to Abdillah ibn Nafi, and Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Malik, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, that she informed him from Habibah bint Sahl al-Ansariyyah, that she was under Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, and that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the dawn prayer and found Habibah bint Sahl at his door in the darkness. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is this? She said: I am Habibah bint Sahl. He said: What is your matter? She said: Neither I nor Thabit ibn Qays - meaning her husband. When Thabit came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: This is Habibah bint Sahl, and she has mentioned what Allah willed that she mention. So Habibah said: O Messenger of Allah, all that he gave me is with me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Thabit: Take from her. So he took from her, and she remained among her family."
"778","Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us, he said: Qurad Abu Nuh narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), she said: The wife of Thabit ibn Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: I blame nothing of Thabit in religion or character, but I fear disbelief in Islam. So he said: Will you return to him his garden? She said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to return to him his garden, and he separated between them."
"779","Abu Muhammad said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman also narrated it, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), except that he did not mention at its end: and he separated between them. Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated it to us, from his father, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"780","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best charity is what is given out of sufficiency, and begin with those you support. Abu Hurayrah said: Your wife says: Spend on me or divorce me; and your child says: Spend on me, to whom do you leave me? And your servant says: Spend on me or sell me."
